SUMMARY:Jazz at Lincoln Center Presents World on a String: Swinging Songs
  of Broadway
DESCRIPTION:Marking the fifth production in the Jazz at Lincoln Center PR
 ESENTS series\, guest vocalists Kate Kortum and David Marino will debut a
 rrangements of tunes from Broadway's most beloved productions including H
 amilton\, Wicked\, South Pacific\, West Side Story\, and more in a specia
 l concert event entitled World on a String: Swinging Songs of Broadway.  
 &#160\;  For over three decades\, Jazz at Lincoln Center has been a leadi
 ng advocate for jazz\, culture\, and arts education globally. Under the d
 irection of Wynton Marsalis\, Jazz at Lincoln Center has brought the art 
 form of jazz from the heart of New York City to over 446 cities in more t
 han 40 countries.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Marking the fifth production in the Jaz
 z at Lincoln Center PRESENTS series\, guest vocalists Kate Kortum and Dav
 id Marino will debut arrangements of tunes from Broadway's most beloved p
 roductions including <i>Hamilton</i>\, <i>Wicked</i>\, <i>South Pacific</
 i>\, <i>West Side Story</i>\, and more in a special concert event entitle
 d <i>World on a String: Swinging Songs of Broadway</i>.</p><p>  &#160\;</
 p><p>  For over three decades\, Jazz at Lincoln Center has been a leading
  advocate for jazz\, culture\, and arts education globally. Under the dir
 ection of Wynton Marsalis\, Jazz at Lincoln Center has brought the art fo
 rm of jazz from the heart of New York City to over 446 cities in more tha
 n 40 countries.</p>
